  /// When the job reached a terminal state; absent while running.
  final DateTime? finishedAt;

  /// What a finished job did, once it records a summary. A `scan` counts files:
  /// `audioFiles` (every audio file it visited) is `created`, `updated`,
  /// `sidecarsUpdated` (a lyrics, cue or cover change without the audio
  /// changing), `copies` (files that joined an item as another copy of its
  /// audio or another encoding of its recording), `unchanged` and `errored`
  /// together, and `filesSeen` is `audioFiles` and `skipped` (files that are
  /// not audio). `relinked` (moved or renamed) and `reread` (read in full
  /// rather than recognized by size and time) count among the audio files;
  /// `missing` counts items whose files are gone, `promoted` copies that took a
  /// gone file's place, `dropped` the records of gone files removed, and
  /// `walkErrors` entries the scan could not read, which no file count holds.
  /// `rootUnreachable` says a library's folder could not be reached, so nothing
  /// under it was marked missing, and `subPathGone` that the folder asked for
  /// was not there. For administrators, `runs` lists each library's own counts
  /// in the same words, with its `libraryPid` and `library` name, and
  /// `rootsUnreachable` names the libraries whose folder could not be reached.
  /// An `analyze` pass reports `analyzed`, `loudnessMeasured`, `measureFailed`,
  /// `skipped` and `errored`, with `fingerprintFallbacks` (files fpcalc could
  /// not read, fingerprinted another way that does not group with fpcalc's) and
  /// `fingerprintPartialReads` (fpcalc reads kept although they ended in an
  /// error, their fingerprint covering the span analyzed); an `enrich` pass the
  /// same tallies as the enrichment status's `lastRun`; an `organize` run
  /// `profile` (absent when it laid several libraries out by their own),
  /// `moved`, `skipped` (files that did not move, in place or held back),
  /// `held` (of those, the moves held back), `errored`, `sidecarsMoved` and
  /// `dirsPruned` (folders the moves emptied and removed), and an
  /// `organize-undo` moving one back the same without `profile`. A `set-kind`
  /// run reports `converted` (the items that changed kind in place), `absorbed`
